 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "a19c78ce",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "<div style=\"border-top:4px solid #0f766e;padding:16px\">DATA WAREHOUSING WITH APACHE DORIS · OPTIONAL LAB</div>\n",
    "\n",
    "# Optional Lab 5B: MySQL → Flink CDC → Doris\n",
    "\n",
    "Verify the initial snapshot, inserts, updates, deletes, checkpoints, and a controlled stop followed by savepoint restoration and catch-up.\n",
    "Allow 35–50 minutes. Module 7 can reuse this lab; it is not required for main-course completion.\n",
    "\n",
    "Read the [environment guide](../../environments/streaming/README.md) first. The lab starts course MySQL and Flink JobManager/TaskManager services and reuses the Doris sandbox.\n",
    "The first cell checks Docker capacity and applies the streaming resource overlay (12 GiB Doris memory cap). Applying the overlay to an existing sandbox may recreate its container while preserving its named volumes: finish other course work first.\n",
    "It rebuilds only `dw_course_l1_streaming.ext_cdc_orders` and clears the dedicated MySQL `course_cdc.orders` table before inserting three simulated orders.\n",
    "These are not WWI historical orders and do not use the main-course amount baseline. Do not run concurrent instances in the same sandbox. Use only the demonstration accounts, never production systems.\n",
    "This is **single-table SQL synchronization with a fixed schema**, not whole-database synchronization or automatic schema evolution."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "87e994b4",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "import os, sys\n",
    "from uuid import uuid4\n",
    "course = next(p for p in [Path.cwd(), *Path.cwd().parents] if (p / \"dw_course\").is_dir())\n",
    "sys.path.insert(0, str(course))\n",
    "from dw_course.docker_runtime import prepare_environment, connect_sandbox\n",
    "from dw_course.runtime import expect\n",
    "from dw_course.ui import show_response, show_records\n",
    "from dw_course.streaming import (\n",
    "    prepare_streaming, kafka, produce, mysql, flink_api, submit_sql,\n",
    "    wait_checkpoint, stop_with_savepoint, wait_rows, check_flink_job, check_routine_load,\n",
    "    cleanup_cdc_jobs,\n",
    ")\n",
    "prepare_environment(start=True, streaming=True, streaming_profile="cdc")\n",
    "os.environ[\"DW_DATABASE\"] = \"dw_course_l1_streaming\"\n",
    "lab = connect_sandbox()\n",
    "print(\"Isolated lab database:\", lab.database)\n",
    "\n",
    "prepare_streaming(\"cdc\", start=True)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "42256e90",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Check for active jobs and initialize source and target\n",
    "\n",
    "The setup cell automatically cancels stale jobs named `course_mysql_orders` before resetting the source and target. It refuses to touch any other active Flink job. Use the savepoint stop flow below when you intend to resume an existing experiment.\n",
    "The source uses ROW/FULL Binlog and a CDC user with read and replication privileges. The target uses a Merge-on-Write Unique Key table."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "0939a5d4",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "cleanup_cdc_jobs()\n",
    "active = [j for j in flink_api(\"/jobs/overview\")[\"jobs\"] if j[\"state\"] not in {\"FINISHED\",\"CANCELED\",\"FAILED\"}]\n",
    "expect(active, [])\n",
    "mysql(\"\"\"DELETE FROM course_cdc.orders;\n",
    "INSERT INTO course_cdc.orders VALUES\n",
    "(920001,1,'CREATED',100.00),(920002,2,'CREATED',200.00),(920003,3,'CREATED',50.00);\n",
    "SHOW MASTER STATUS;\n",
    "SELECT * FROM course_cdc.orders ORDER BY order_id;\"\"\")\n",
    "lab.execute(\"DROP TABLE IF EXISTS ext_cdc_orders\")\n",
    "lab.execute(\"\"\"CREATE TABLE ext_cdc_orders (\n",
    "    order_id BIGINT NOT NULL, customer_id BIGINT NOT NULL,\n",
    "    order_status VARCHAR(32) NOT NULL, order_amount DECIMAL(18,2) NOT NULL\n",
    ") UNIQUE KEY(order_id) DISTRIBUTED BY HASH(order_id) BUCKETS 1\n",
    "PROPERTIES(\"replication_num\"=\"1\", \"enable_unique_key_merge_on_write\"=\"true\")\"\"\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "62b6e58a",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Submit snapshot and incremental synchronization SQL\n",
    "\n",
    "Use a unique sink label prefix for each new experiment. Restore with the same SQL, parallelism, and prefix.\n",
    "Enable checkpoints and sink 2PC. The INSERT starts a continuous job; RUNNING alone does not prove synchronization.\n",
    "The initial image build downloads three JARs; pinned versions are listed in the environment guide.\n",
    "Data and checkpoint waits check job health and report terminal failures with a link to the job's exception page."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "f525fd18",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "label = \"course_cdc_\" + uuid4().hex[:12]\n",
    "sql = f\"\"\"SET 'execution.checkpointing.interval' = '5s';\n",
    "SET 'parallelism.default' = '1';\n",
    "SET 'pipeline.name' = 'course_mysql_orders';\n",
    "CREATE TABLE mysql_orders (\n",
    " order_id BIGINT, customer_id BIGINT, order_status STRING, order_amount DECIMAL(18,2),\n",
    " PRIMARY KEY(order_id) NOT ENFORCED\n",
    ") WITH (\n",
    " 'connector'='mysql-cdc','hostname'='mysql','port'='3306',\n",
    " 'username'='course_cdc','password'='course_cdc_local_only',\n",
    " 'database-name'='course_cdc','table-name'='orders','server-id'='55101-55102',\n",
    " 'server-time-zone'='Asia/Shanghai','scan.startup.mode'='initial'\n",
    ");\n",
    "CREATE TABLE doris_orders (\n",
    " order_id BIGINT, customer_id BIGINT, order_status STRING, order_amount DECIMAL(18,2),\n",
    " PRIMARY KEY(order_id) NOT ENFORCED\n",
    ") WITH (\n",
    " 'connector'='doris','fenodes'='doris:8030','benodes'='doris:8040','auto-redirect'='false','table.identifier'='dw_course_l1_streaming.ext_cdc_orders',\n",
    " 'username'='root','password'='', 'sink.label-prefix'='{label}',\n",
    " 'sink.enable-delete'='true','sink.enable-2pc'='true',\n",
    " 'sink.properties.format'='json','sink.properties.read_json_by_line'='true'\n",
    ");\n",
    "INSERT INTO doris_orders SELECT order_id,customer_id,order_status,order_amount FROM mysql_orders;\n",
    "\"\"\"\n",
    "print(sql)\n",
    "job_id = submit_sql(sql)\n",
    "print(\"Job ID:\", job_id)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "f7a0d5a0",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "baseline = [[920001,1,\"CREATED\",\"100.00\"],[920002,2,\"CREATED\",\"200.00\"],[920003,3,\"CREATED\",\"50.00\"]]\n",
    "expect(wait_rows(lab,\"ext_cdc_orders\",baseline, check_health=lambda: check_flink_job(job_id)),baseline)\n",
    "show_records(\"Completed checkpoint\", [(wait_checkpoint(job_id)[\"latest\"][\"completed\"],)], columns=[\"Completed checkpoints\"])\n",
    "lab.sql(\"SELECT * FROM ext_cdc_orders ORDER BY order_id\", title=\"Snapshot results\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "6088c0dc",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Change the source and verify real Binlog inserts, updates, and deletes\n",
    "\n",
    "Update 920001, delete 920002, and insert 920004. Deletion comes from a source event, not a DELETE executed against Doris by the notebook.\n",
    "Expect three rows totaling 225.00. Inspect the current MySQL data and Binlog file position as well."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "7621ba57",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "mysql(\"\"\"UPDATE course_cdc.orders SET order_status='PAID' WHERE order_id=920001;\n",
    "DELETE FROM course_cdc.orders WHERE order_id=920002;\n",
    "INSERT INTO course_cdc.orders VALUES (920004,4,'CREATED',75.00);\n",
    "SELECT * FROM course_cdc.orders ORDER BY order_id;\n",
    "SHOW MASTER STATUS;\"\"\")\n",
    "changed = [[920001,1,\"PAID\",\"100.00\"],[920003,3,\"CREATED\",\"50.00\"],[920004,4,\"CREATED\",\"75.00\"]]\n",
    "expect(wait_rows(lab,\"ext_cdc_orders\",changed, check_health=lambda: check_flink_job(job_id)),changed)\n",
    "expect(lab.query(\"SELECT COUNT(*),SUM(order_amount) FROM ext_cdc_orders\"),[[3,\"225.00\"]])"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "d5f1f84f",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Save state and stop while source writes continue\n",
    "\n",
    "This is a **controlled savepoint stop and restore**, not a node crash or automatic failover experiment.\n",
    "The savepoint contains source consumption progress and operator state. `SHOW MASTER STATUS` shows the current source end position; it cannot replace the job's saved consumption position.\n",
    "Do not delete Binlog files, the MySQL volume, or the Flink state volume."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "17644ac2",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "savepoint = stop_with_savepoint(job_id)\n",
    "print(\"Savepoint path:\", savepoint)\n",
    "mysql(\"\"\"UPDATE course_cdc.orders SET order_amount=125.00 WHERE order_id=920001;\n",
    "DELETE FROM course_cdc.orders WHERE order_id=920003;\n",
    "INSERT INTO course_cdc.orders VALUES (920005,5,'CREATED',40.00);\n",
    "SHOW MASTER STATUS;\"\"\")\n",
    "expect(lab.query(\"SELECT * FROM ext_cdc_orders ORDER BY order_id\"), changed)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "4509d5c5",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5. Restore saved state and catch up\n",
    "\n",
    "Add only the restoration path and reuse the original SQL. Do not reinitialize the source or target.\n",
    "Expect three rows totaling 240.00, with the PAID status preserved. Verify Flink's restored checkpoint information, not just the final row count."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "3e2ed042",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "restored_job = submit_sql(f\"SET 'execution.savepoint.path' = '{savepoint}';\\n\" + sql)\n",
    "final = [[920001,1,\"PAID\",\"125.00\"],[920004,4,\"CREATED\",\"75.00\"],[920005,5,\"CREATED\",\"40.00\"]]\n",
    "expect(wait_rows(lab,\"ext_cdc_orders\",final, check_health=lambda: check_flink_job(restored_job)),final)\n",
    "checkpoints = wait_checkpoint(restored_job)\n",
    "restored = checkpoints[\"latest\"][\"restored\"]\n",
    "expect(restored[\"external_path\"],savepoint)\n",
    "show_response(restored, title=\"Restoration record\")\n",
    "expect(lab.query(\"SELECT COUNT(*),SUM(order_amount) FROM ext_cdc_orders\"),[[3,\"240.00\"]])\n",
    "mysql(\"SELECT * FROM course_cdc.orders ORDER BY order_id\")\n",
    "lab.sql(\"SELECT * FROM ext_cdc_orders ORDER BY order_id\", title=\"Results after restoration\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "7f444ccf",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 6. Stop this job and retain evidence\n",
    "\n",
    "Submit the initial snapshot, insert/update/delete results, savepoint path, restored checkpoint information, and final results.\n",
    "This lab covers normal operation and controlled restoration. It does not prove exactly-once behavior for every failure path, or cover out-of-order events, atomic visibility across tables, or production concurrency.\n",
    "\n",
    "Independent exercise: stop the job, change another order, restore from the new savepoint, and explain why business update timestamps cannot replace consumption positions.\n",
    "After finishing, stop the course services as described in the README. Data volumes are not deleted automatically."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "16438133",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "final_savepoint = stop_with_savepoint(restored_job)\n",
    "print(\"Final savepoint path:\",final_savepoint)\n",
    "lab.close()"
   ]
  }
 ],
